We are pleased to submit our manuscript entitled "Effectiveness of Temporary Portable Rumble Strips in Utah" to the Transportation Research Board for consideration for publication in Transportation Research Record.

The manuscript describes the results of a field experiment with TPRS installed with varying spacing at four sites in Utah. The findings of the experiment suggest that TPRS is not as effective at reducing driver speeds as previous studies have shown. This is also the first study we are aware of that examines the risk to workers who must enter the road to adjust the strips.

An earlier, non-peer-reviewed report presenting findings from this study was
published by the project sponsor, the Utah Department of Transportation 
#link("https://rosap.ntl.bts.gov/view/dot/91241"). The present manuscript draws
on the same study and dataset but has been substantially revised and developed
for an academic audience.

We believe that this research is of interest to the TRB community and we look forward to receiving reviews of the manuscript.

